  "fromId": "t",
  "toId": "t_retroflex",
  "preamble": "Retroflexion of the alveolar or dental stop [t] to [ʈ]. In Indo-Aryan it is a progressive assimilation: after the retroflex sibilant [ʂ] (itself from the RUKI change and from Indo-Iranian *š), a following *t became ṭ, so Proto-Indo-Iranian *Haštā́ 'eight' gives Sanskrit aṣṭā́ against Avestan ašta. Cluster coalescence such as Scandinavian rt > ʈ and Tibetan tr- > ʈʂ is a different process and is not included.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Retroflexion, Assimilation",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Sanskrit",
      "languageFamily": "Indo-Aryan",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Proto-Indo-Iranian *Haštā́ 'eight'",
          "to": "aṣṭā́ / aṣṭá [ɐʂʈaː]",
          "note": "The *t retroflexed after the preceding retroflex sibilant; Avestan ašta keeps t."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Indo-Iranian *Hištás 'desired'",
          "to": "iṣṭá",
          "note": "Avestan išta keeps t."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Indo-Iranian *dr̥štás 'seen'",
          "to": "dṛṣṭá",
          "note": "Past participle of dṛś 'see' with the suffix -ta."
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Indo-Iranian *naštás 'lost'",
          "to": "naṣṭá",
          "note": "Avestan našta keeps t."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
